---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="You Found the Still Point"
  description="You're holding one of the coins. Here's what the dish in the middle is for, and where to go next if you want more."
>
  <!-- Page Header -->
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="page-header-content">
      <span class="coin-face" aria-hidden="true"><span class="coin-stone"></span></span>
      <h1>You found the still point.</h1>
      <p class="epigraph">
        <em>Somebody handed you a coin. Nothing is being asked of you.</em><br>
        <em>This page is just here in case you wanted to know what it was.</em>
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="found-content">

    <!-- The object -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>The object</h2>

      <p>The dish in the middle is a still point. It's meant to be rubbed with a thumb — that's the
      whole design. Something with a little weight to it that lives in a pocket and gives your hand
      somewhere to go when your head is going somewhere else.</p>

      <p>The front is deliberately wordless. An object that explains itself gets a glance. One that
      doesn't gets a question.</p>

      <p>The back is the only instruction there is: <strong>find a third way</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- The line -->
    <section class="section">
      <blockquote class="handoff">
        When you're stuck on a binary, one thing or the other, remember to be still, and maybe the
        third way will come to you.
      </blockquote>
    </section>

    <!-- Third way -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>A third way to what?</h2>

      <p>Mostly: to whatever you've been handed as a choice between two things. The frame is usually
      the problem before either option is.</p>

      <p>The question this project started from is a specific one — how to live well alongside
      machines that keep getting more capable, without either handing them everything or refusing
      them outright. But the move is older and wider than that, and it isn't a position to agree
      with. It's a thing to do with five seconds and a thumb.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Where to go -->
    <section class="section next-steps">
      <h2>If you want more</h2>

      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li><a href="/practice">The practice</a> — three units, each one teachable in a breath.
        The still point you're holding is the first of them.</li>
        <li><a href="https://forum.stillpointproject.org">The forum</a> — somewhere to think out
        loud with other people. It's early: one welcome post, one open room. The first few people
        in help shape what it becomes, which is an honest description and not a sales pitch.</li>
        <li><a href="/stories">The stories</a> — there's fiction here too, near-future, about a
        world that relearns how to be still. Doors into the same question. Free to read.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="quiet-note">The coins come in two batches — green ones from earlier this year, black
      ones with a red stone since. The back of the green ones says <em>let's find a third way</em>.
      Printed before the wording got simplified. Same idea, one fewer word.</p>
    </section>

  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  @import '../styles/design-tokens.css';

  /* Page Header */
  /* Extra top padding so the coin graphic clears the fixed navbar. */
  .page-header {
    text-align: center;
    padding: calc(var(--space-3xl) + 3rem) var(--space-lg) var(--space-2xl);
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* The coin, drawn: black face, red stone at the still point. */
  .coin-face {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 4.5rem;
    height: 4.5rem;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-lg);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #121212;
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1),
      0 6px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
  }

  .coin-stone {
    width: 1.8rem;
    height: 1.8rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 40% 35%, #e05a4e, #b23a30);
    box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 5vw, 2.6rem);
    color: var(--color-heading);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-lg);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .epigraph {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.5vw, 1.25rem);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* Main Content */
  .found-content {
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-lg) var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .section {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-2xl);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }

  .section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    color: var(--color-heading);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-lg);
  }

  .section p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .section strong {
    color: var(--color-accent-1);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .section a {
    color: var(--color-accent-1);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* The handoff line — the only thing on this page worth memorising */
  .handoff {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-heading);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-1);
    padding: var(--space-md) 0 var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Plain list — matches the practice page */
  .plain-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-md) 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .plain-list li {
    color: var(--color-text);
    padding: var(--space-sm) 0;
    padding-left: 1.5em;
    position: relative;
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }

  .plain-list li::before {
    content: '—';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-accent-1);
  }

  .quiet-note {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }
</style>
